        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dendrochronology: Tree Rings, Climate Records, Cross-Dating",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A second proxy variable: the maximum X-ray density of the latewood zone. MXD is a stronger temperature signal than ring width for many high-latitude/high-altitude conifers — specifically capturing **late-summer temperature**. Used in the Northern Hemisphere temperature reconstructions (Briffa et al., Science 1998)."
    },
    {
