        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### COFECHA and Statistical Cross-Dating"
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md#031",
      "path": [
        "03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:dendrology:03-dendrochronology, git-history:dendrology:03-dendrochronology]",
        "canonical_path": "dendrology/03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md",
        "concepts": "[dendrochronology]",
        "current_path": "dendrology/03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md",
        "id": "maxim:dendrology:dendrochronology",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "dendrology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[dendrochronology]",
        "section": "dendrology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Dendrochronology: Tree Rings, Climate Records, Cross-Dating",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Modern cross-dating uses software (COFECHA) that computes Pearson correlations between 50-year overlapping windows of each series against the master chronology. Acceptable correlation threshold typically r > 0.3 (p < 0.01), but for confident dating r > 0.5 preferred."
    },
    {
      "id": "03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md#032",
      "path": [
        "03-DENDROCHRONOLOGY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
